  "worked_solution": "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $4∣12.$ Therefore, we have\n$4∣12$ and $12∣h,$ which implies that $4∣h.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $2∣4.$ Therefore, we have\n$2∣4$ and $4∣h,$ which implies that $2∣h.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $h=3.$ Then, $3∣3$ but $12∤3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
